/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 108 0 R
/T (Across all four study countries notably Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, key informants consistently identified women as the principal holders and transmitters of practical ecological knowledge, including reading weather and seasonal patterns, tracking water source reliability, identifying edible and medicinal plants, managing seed varieties, and recognizing early signs of livestock illness or pasture degradation. This knowledge is typically acquired through direct, sustained daily engagement with the environment over decades, and is transmitted informally from older to younger women rather than through any formal institution.)
/E (Across all four study countries notably Kenya, Somalia, Tanzania and South Africa, key informants consistently identified women as the principal holders and transmitters of practical ecological knowledge, including reading weather and seasonal patterns, tracking water source reliability, identifying edible and medicinal plants, managing seed varieties, and recognizing early signs of livestock illness or pasture degradation. This knowledge is typically acquired through direct, sustained daily engagement with the environment over decades, and is transmitted informally from older to younger women rather than through any formal institution.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [4]
>>
