/E (This finding is well supported in the wider literature. The World Bank \(2022\) documents Indigenous women's climate knowledge as the product of generational transfer that has made women climate experts, innovators, and problem-solvers in their communities, while research from Baringo County \(Liru, 2026\) documents specific hybrid practices which include informal women-led weather-scouting networks that combine this indigenous knowledge base with newer digital tools.)
