283 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 112 0 R
/E (The recommendations below are derived directly from the key informant interview findings presented in this brief and are further supported by the regional and global literature reviewed above. They translate this brief's core argument i.e. that women's adaptation leadership is already extensive but structurally under-financed.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
284 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 112 0 R
/T (1. Direct Climate Finance)
/E (1. Direct Climate Finance)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
285 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 616 0 R
/E (Fund women-led adaptation directly, at scale - create dedicated, flexible, multi-year funding windows for women's savings groups, cooperatives and community-based organizations, reducing reliance on intermediated funding structures that dilute resources before they reach the community level.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
286 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 617 0 R
/E <>
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
287 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 618 0 R
/E (Track and close the climate-finance gap - establish standing monitoring indicators for the share of climate finance reaching women-led and women-designed adaptation initiatives specifically, given that an estimated 0.01 percent of global climate finance currently reaches Indigenous women-led initiatives directly. )
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
288 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 112 0 R
/T (2. Livestock-Centered Livelihood Diversification)
/E (2. Livestock-Centered Livelihood Diversification)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
289 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 619 0 R
/E (Prioritize diversification that strengthens pastoralism rather than replaces it - support herd splitting, species diversification and livestock value-chain development \(milk processing, hides, off-take\) as the first line of diversification for women-led households, since evidence shows non-pastoral diversification succeeds primarily where market access, credit and infrastructure are already adequate such that without these preconditions, diversification tends to be distress-driven rather than strategic.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
290 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 620 0 R
/E (Scale index-based livestock insurance \(IBLI\) - expand forecast-triggered insurance instruments that pay out on pre-agreed climate indices before livestock losses occur, protecting the herd asset itself and reducing pressure on women to sell down breeding stock during drought.)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
291 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 112 0 R
/T (POLICY RECOMMENDATIONS)
/E (POLICY RECOMMENDATIONS)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
